This driver provides support for modern Realtek multi-gigabit Ethernet
controllers (RTL8125, RTL8126, RTL8127).

It is implemented as a separate driver rather than extending rge(4D)
due to differences in hardware initialization, DMA behavior, interrupt
handling, and descriptor formats.

The driver integrates with the illumos GLDv3 MAC framework and supports
MSI/MSI-X interrupts, multi-queue RX/TX rings, and basic offload
capabilities.


Initialization model
--------------------

Hardware initialization is divided into two stages:

1. Vendor initialization
2. Driver-controlled initialization

Vendor initialization consists of sequences derived from reference
implementations and is treated as opaque.  This code is not modified
unless required for correct operation.

Driver-controlled initialization includes:

- interrupt setup
- ring allocation
- DMA setup
- MAC configuration

This separation simplifies maintenance and reduces risk when updating
support for new hardware revisions.


Interrupt model
---------------

The driver supports the following interrupt modes:

- MSI-X (preferred)
- MSI
- MSI with timer-based interrupt fallback

Timer mode generates periodic interrupts and may provide stable
throughput, but can limit maximum packet rate under high PPS workloads.

Under load, interrupt frequency may decrease when operating in
timer-based mode.


Hardware considerations
-----------------------

Known hardware-specific behaviors include:

- Variation in interrupt register layout across revisions
- DMA ordering constraints on certain revisions
- UDP checksum offload limitations on early RTL8125 devices


Stop and shutdown
-----------------

The stop sequence is ordered to avoid deadlocks:

1. Mark device as stopping
2. Disable interrupts
3. Release driver mutex
4. Wait for taskq and interrupt handlers to complete
5. Drain RX/TX rings
6. Re-acquire mutex and release resources

Waiting for taskq completion must not be performed while holding the
driver mutex, as interrupt handlers may require the same lock.


Driver development notes
------------------------

Parts of the initialization logic are derived from existing drivers,
including:

- FreeBSD kernel (src/sys/dev/rge/)
- FreeBSD re_kmod
- Linux rtl8125/rtl8126/rtl8127 drivers
- Vendor-provided driver sources

The code in the "core" directory is organized into two categories:

1. Directly imported code with naming adjustments
2. Modified or reimplemented functionality

The following files are derived from FreeBSD sources with naming
adaptation (rge_ → re_, RGE_ → RE_):

    if_re_hw.h
    if_re_hw.c
    if_re_microcode.h
    if_re_vendor.h
    if_rereg.h
    if_revar.h

Some files may include minor adjustments (e.g. logging or additional
register definitions).

Modified or reimplemented components include:

    re_chip.h
    re_chip.c


Implementation details
----------------------

FreeBSD MII register definitions have been replaced with illumos MII
definitions.

The following functions are based on or derived from existing drivers:

- re_check_mac_version()
  Derived from FreeBSD re_kmod and identification logic in rge_attach().

- re_setup_interrupt_mask()
  Implemented to match behavior observed in vendor drivers RTL8125/8126/8127.

- re_init_software_variable()
  Derived from vendor driver logic; configuration values must match
  hardware expectations.

The following functions originate from the FreeBSD rge(4) driver and have
been adapted for illumos:

- re_init_locked()
- re_stop_locked()

These implementations were modified to integrate with the illumos driver
model, including changes to locking, interrupt handling, and datapath
control. Additional adjustments were made based on analysis of behavior
observed in vendor drivers.

Other parts of the driver are derived from vendor implementations and
adapted for illumos integration.
